# fixedbugs, defect 2034, 2026-10-12, a shape beside the 569 format case.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own whose `vprintf` wrapper is declared
# `__attribute__((format(printf, 1, 2)))`, called with a `char *` for `%d`,
# built and printed a pointer's low bits (1742570, then 36476650) at exit
# 0: the attribute makes clang judge the wrapper's call as it judges
# `printf`'s, and the region ignored that judgement with the rest of `-Wall`.
#
# FIX: `-Wformat` stays an error in the region (`emit/header_region.hero`'s
# `KEPT`), so the attributed wrapper is refused at the header's line 6. A
# wrapper with no attribute is not seen by clang at all, and builds.

extern "fixedbugs-2034-a-header-s-own-printf-wrapper-with-a-format-attribute-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function fmt_shout() -> i32

function main()
    print(fmt_shout())
